  "https://atomicdata.dev/properties/description": "The shape, as JSON whose layout depends on the geometry kind. Metres, local to the storey, Z up; heights are above the storey floor. wallAxis {start: [x, y], end: [x, y], height, thickness, base?}: a straight wall centred on its axis. extrusion {polygon: [[x, y], ...], depth, base?}: a polygon pushed up by depth from base; base defaults to -depth for an IfcSlab (top flush with the floor) and to 0 otherwise. Floors, flat roofs with their overhang, columns, piers, chimneys, built-in furniture. opening {offset, width, height, sill}: a door or window in its host wall, offset metres from the wall start. stair {start: [x, y], direction, width, rise, risers, going, base?}: a straight flight starting at start, going direction degrees counter-clockwise from +X, climbing rise metres in risers equal steps over going metres. mesh {file, at?: [x, y, z], rotation?}: a glTF/GLB File resource placed at at, rotated rotation degrees around Z. Checked by the app, not by the server.",
